@startuml msb_flow
title paddock: an msb session, from boot to collected (SPEC 2.2)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

actor User
participant "cli.py\n`paddock launch <profile>\n~--backend msb`" as CLI
participant "sessions.py" as Sessions
participant "backends/microsandbox.py" as Backend
participant "herdr_client.py" as Client
participant "Herdr" as Herdr
participant "synth_config.py" as Synth
participant "msb\n(one host process per VM)" as Msb
participant "guest\n(microVM from the agent's image)" as Guest

== create the session ==

User -> CLI : paddock launch msb-live ~--backend msb
CLI -> Sessions : launch(profile, name, backend="msb")
activate Sessions
Sessions -> Sessions : create_session(profile, name, "msb")\nbackend_for("msb") -> the microsandbox module
Sessions -> Backend : prepare(profile)
activate Backend
Backend -> Backend : the agent needs an `image` in the registry\n(an agent without one is refused here, before a VM exists:\nthe guest holds what the image holds. `shell` gets alpine)
Backend -> Backend : new_run_dir() -> <state>/runs/<timestamp>-<rand>/\nvm_handle -> paddock-<that directory's name>\nworkdir_for(profile) -> shared_dir, else run_dir/work,\nresolved, because msb mounts the source as written
Backend -> Synth : build(profile, agent, run_dir,\nguest_dir="/paddock-config", defer_credentials=True)
activate Synth
Synth -> Synth : run_dir/config: the ticked skills, the generated MCP\nwhitelist, the config the agent rewrites. COPIED, not linked:\na link to a host path is outside the mount (SPEC 4.3).\nNO TOKEN YET: everything below can still fail.
Synth --> Backend : dir (host side), env {CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/paddock-config},\nargs ~--mcp-config /paddock-config/.mcp.json ~--strict-mcp-config
deactivate Synth
Backend -> Msb : msb create ~--name paddock-<run>\n~--mount-dir <resolved workdir>:/work ~--workdir /work\n[~--mount-dir <run_dir>/config:/paddock-config-src:ro\n-e CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/paddock-config]\n~--net-default deny [~--net-rule allow@dns\n~--net-rule allow@<domain>:tcp:443 per allowed domain]\n<image from the agent entry, else alpine>
activate Msb
Msb -> Guest : boot (175ms to usable, measured in the spike)
activate Guest
Msb --> Backend : created
Backend -> Msb : msb exec ~--timeout 110s paddock-<run> ~-- /bin/sh -c\n`command -v claude >/dev/null 2>&1 || npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code@<pinned>`\n(skipped when the agent has no `install`)
Msb -> Guest : install the agent (about 21s, measured)
note right
  Once per SESSION, not once per image: a new sandbox is
  a fresh clone, so msb's layer cache saves the 20s pull
  and not the install. The install downloads over the same
  deny-by-default network, so the profile has to allow the
  registry, and msb cannot withdraw that rule afterwards.

  A profile without the npm preset spends about 70s here
  and then fails. The chooser says so twice before the
  wait, on the confirm and on the progress screen, and
  draws the failure on a screen of its own rather than
  printing it into a popup that is already closing.
end note
Backend -> Synth : place_credentials(profile, agent, run_dir)
activate Synth
Synth -> Synth : NOW write run_dir/config/.credentials.json, 0600.\nThe agent exists in the guest, so a token can be of use to it.
deactivate Synth
Backend -> Msb : msb exec ~--timeout 110s paddock-<run> ~-- /bin/sh -c\n`mkdir -p /paddock-config && cp -a /paddock-config-src/. /paddock-config/`
Msb -> Guest : the guest takes its own copy, on its own filesystem
note right
  From here the guest reads and writes /paddock-config,
  which is the overlay. The read-only mount is a source,
  never a destination: nothing the agent writes to its
  config reaches the host, and none of it survives the VM.

  Anything that fails from `msb create` on: delete the
  token, remove the VM, then raise. The session is not
  registered yet, so nothing else would collect either.
  BaseException, not Exception: ctrl-c lands in this
  window nearly every time, and catching only Exception
  left a microVM running that nothing would collect.
  A process killed outright rolls nothing back, so
  `paddock gc` sweeps `msb ls` for paddock-<run> handles
  the registry does not claim (SPEC section 8).
end note
Backend -> Backend : write run_dir/launch.sh:\n`msb exec ~--tty paddock-<run> [~-- claude <config flags>]`\nwrite run_dir/launch.json: vm_handle, workdir, command
Backend --> Sessions : Run(run_dir, workdir, vm_handle, command)
deactivate Backend
Sessions -> Sessions : register in <state>/sessions.json\nwith backend="msb" and vm_handle

== attach a tab (once now, again for every later tab) ==

Sessions -> Backend : load_run(run_dir) then open_pane(run, label="sbx:<session>")
activate Backend
Backend -> Client : create_tab(workdir, label)
note right
  The tab's own cwd is the HOST side of the mount,
  so the pane and the guest shell see the same files.
  No env is passed: a variable set on `msb create`
  with -e reaches every later exec, the interactive
  shell included. Verified on msb 0.6.13.
end note
Client -> Herdr : herdr tab create ~--cwd <workdir> ~--label sbx:<session> ~--focus
Herdr --> Client : {"result":{"root_pane":{"pane_id":"wA:pA"}}}
Backend -> Client : run_in_pane("wA:pA", launch_line(run_dir))
Client -> Herdr : herdr pane run wA:pA\n`exec /bin/sh <run_dir>/launch.sh`
deactivate Backend
Herdr -> Msb : the pane's shell runs\n`msb exec ~--tty paddock-<run> [~-- claude <config flags>]`
Msb -> Guest : exec with a PTY (20ms), in the same process namespace\nas every other tab on this session
Guest --> User : the agent, or the image's own shell, at /work.\nThe agent reads its credentials and skills\nfrom /paddock-config and writes back there,\nwhich is the run dir on the host.
Sessions --> CLI : (session, "wA:pA")
deactivate Sessions

== collect the session ==

User -> Herdr : closes the last tab on the session
note right
  Nothing tells paddock. herdr has pane events on
  its socket, but no paddock process is running to
  hear them, so the VM keeps running until the next
  paddock command reconciles (SPEC 3.4).
end note

User -> CLI : the next paddock command:\nchoose, launch, attach,\nor `paddock gc` on its own
CLI -> Sessions : reconcile()
activate Sessions
Sessions -> Client : list_pane_ids()
Client -> Herdr : herdr pane list
Herdr --> Client : {"result":{"panes":[...]}}, no wA:pA among them
Sessions -> Sessions : the pane list and the registry are both read\nunder the registry lock, so a tab another paddock\nopened a moment ago is in both and never reads as closed
Sessions -> Sessions : wA:pA is gone and it was the last one,\nand keep_alive is not set, so drop the session\nfrom the registry
Sessions -> Synth : discard_credentials(run_dir)\n(the copied token must not outlive the session, SPEC 8)
Sessions -> Backend : collect(run_dir, vm_handle)
activate Backend
Backend -> Backend : load_run(run_dir).vm_handle,\nfalling back to the handle the registry kept
Backend -> Msb : msb rm -f paddock-<run>
Msb -> Guest : destroy
deactivate Guest
deactivate Msb
note right
  Always -f: `msb rm` on its own refuses a
  running sandbox (`still running`, exit 1).
  Best effort: reconciling runs ahead of a
  launch and must not break one, so an msb
  that will not answer leaves the VM up and
  the message names the handle and the
  `msb rm -f` that finishes the job.
end note
deactivate Backend
deactivate Sessions

note over Sessions, Guest
  What the run dir keeps: launch.json and launch.sh, config/ for an
  agent session, and work/ when the profile shares no host directory.
  Collecting a session leaves them, because deleting a workdir would
  lose work, but the credential file in config/ goes. config/ is as
  the launcher built it: the guest wrote only to its own copy.

  What the guest never had: the host filesystem. An unmounted path
  is absent, not denied, so there is no PATH shim dir and no
  deny list to get right (SPEC 4.1).
end note

@enduml
